    <statement><p>Without using a calculator, find all solutions to
<m>\displaystyle \cos(\theta) = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}</m> in the interval
<m>0 \leq \theta \leq 2\pi</m>.  If there is more than
one answer, enter your answers as a comma separated list.
Your answers should be exact values (given as fractions,
not decimal approximations).</p>
<p><m>\theta</m> = <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.523599, 5.75959</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



Since <m>\cos(\theta) = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}</m>, we have <m>\theta = \frac{\pi}{6}, \frac{11\pi}{6}</m>.



